  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Regional Migrant Response Plan (RMRP) for Yemen and the Horn of Africa 2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The East and Horn of Africa is a region of origin, transit and destination for hundreds of thousands of migrants, the majority of whom travel in an irregular manner often relying on unscrupulous smugglers to facilitate movement along the Eastern Route with the hope of crossing the Gulf of Yemen and onwards towards the Gulf states with the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia as the main destination for the majority. The persistent vulnerability of migrants in irregular situations is one of the specific drivers of migration and determinants of IOM&#x2019;s response through the Regional Migrant Response Plan (MRP).Through this project, IOM is providing lifesaving assistance to vulnerable migrants and host communities including Voluntary Humanitarian Returns (VHR) and Post Arrival Assistance (PARA).</narrative>
  </description>
